{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486157-suggestions-for-nerfing-v20da-baal-s-caress","id":1486157,"title":"Suggestions for nerfing V20DA Baal's Caress","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-10T09:23:56-07:00","id":1486157,"title":"Suggestions for nerfing V20DA Baal's Caress","content":"So I'm not the biggest fan of Baal's Caress in V20 Core rulebook for modern nights, being that's it's just Protean's feral claws but costs more to get and doesn't last as long (not without significant blood expenditure anyway). DA on the other hand makes an enormous improvement and now it's honestly just too powerful. Willpower's such a cheap and universally beneficial resource so anyone who's invested in it as they probably should can make just about any vampire who isn't maxing out fortitude just explode.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas already on a homebrew nerf (Increase of difficulty on willpower roll, make the bonus last one attack only, base the damage on Quietus rating or blood expenditure or any mixture of these) but I haven't put any into practice so I want to hear other people's ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27401-stygian","name":"Stygian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:44:53-07:00","id":1486372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stygian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486157-suggestions-for-nerfing-v20da-baal-s-caress#post1486157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm not the biggest fan of Baal's Caress in V20 Core rulebook for modern nights, being that's it's just Protean's feral claws but costs more to get and doesn't last as long (not without significant blood expenditure anyway). DA on the other hand makes an enormous improvement and now it's honestly just too powerful. Willpower's such a cheap and universally beneficial resource so anyone who's invested in it as they probably should can make just about any vampire who isn't maxing out fortitude just explode.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas already on a homebrew nerf (Increase of difficulty on willpower roll, make the bonus last one attack only, base the damage on Quietus rating or blood expenditure or any mixture of these) but I haven't put any into practice so I want to hear other people's ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, for once I think Quietus is one of the weakest disciplines in the game, so I really don't see the point in nerfing it. If you want to nerf it and you already ST the modern setting, use the one that is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T04:58:07-07:00","id":1486401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486157-suggestions-for-nerfing-v20da-baal-s-caress?p=1486372#post1486372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, for once I think Quietus is one of the weakest disciplines in the game, so I really don't see the point in nerfing it. If you want to nerf it and you already ST the modern setting, use the one that is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we were to agree that Quietus overall is weak (and I can for modern nights, it becomes an increasingly poor investment after the second power) Dark Ages' version Baal's Caress is still without a doubt the most powerful pre-level 6 power I've ever seen. The ability to convert existing damage into aggravated as well as add on additional damage with a dice pool that can max out at 10 (On one of the cheapest traits to upgrade no less) with a standard difficulty 6 is absurdly strong for a level 4 power. If I were to just use the modern version however, that lands me with the issue you've just mentioned, it's just weak, I want something more in-between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27401,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27401-stygian","user":"Stygian","date":". 07-14-2022, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27401-stygian","name":"Stygian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T06:23:35-07:00","id":1486408,"title":"","content":"Check out my book maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":